#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
ds_research — Source-backed web research delegating to DeepSeek Pro/Flash.

Usage:
  ds_research "query"                         search + fetch + summarise
  ds_research --url URL ["question"]          fetch one URL, answer question
  ds_research --urls URL1,URL2 "q"           fetch explicit URLs + answer
  ds_research --refresh "query"               bypass cache
  ds_research --flash "query"                 use Flash model (cheaper)
  ds_research --limit N "query"               fetch N sources (default 3)
  ds_research --jina-search "query"           force Jina Search (burns ~10k tokens)
  ds_research --deep "query"                  try all providers, up to 3 Jina searches
  ds_research --no-paid-token-providers "q"   disable keyed Jina/Brave/Serper entirely

Search cascade (free-first):
  1. Local source resolver  — installed package source, binary shebang
  2. GitHub API             — repo/README fetch (60 req/hr, no key)
  3. DDGS                   — maintained ddgs package
  4. Jina Search s.jina.ai  — precision fallback; requires JINA_API_KEY;
                              burns ~10k tokens/request; max 1/call by default

Fetch cascade (for URLs):
  1. Jina Reader r.jina.ai  — no key, free
  2. Jina Reader + key      — fallback if rate-limited (burns reader tokens)
  3. Scrapfly               — if SCRAPFLY_API_KEY set
  4. Direct HTTP + bs4      — last resort

Key storage: <this directory>/.env  (chmod 600 attempted)
Cache:       <this directory>/cache/web_research/  (12h TTL)
Logs:        <this directory>/logs/  (API keys redacted)
"""

